  // Note: PyTorch Linear weight shape is (out_features, in_features) = (7,7)
  // Input shape: (6,7)
  // So output = input (6x7) dot weight^T (7x7) = (6x7)
  // We need to transpose weight to get (7x7) -> (7x7) but since weight is square,
  // transpose is the same shape, but we must transpose to match dot_general semantics.

  // Transpose weight from (7,7) to (7,7) (swap dims 0 and 1)
  %weight_t = stablehlo.transpose %arg1 : tensor<7x7xf32> to tensor<7x7xf32> {permutation = [1, 0]}

