func.func @main(%arg0: tensor<6x7x5xf32>, %arg1: tensor<6x6x8xf32>) -> tensor<6x7x20xf32> {
  // %arg0: weight tensor of shape [batch=6, out_channels=7, kernel=5]
  // %arg1: input tensor of shape [batch=6, in_channels=6, length=8]

  // Transposed convolution 1D with dilation=3, stride=1, padding=0
  // StableHLO convolution expects input and kernel in specific layouts.
  // PyTorch ConvTranspose1d weight shape: (in_channels, out_channels, kernel_size)
  // Given %arg0 shape: [6,7,5] which matches (batch=6, out_channels=7, kernel=5)
  // But PyTorch ConvTranspose1d weight shape is (in_channels, out_channels, kernel_size)
  // So %arg0 is actually (in_channels=6, out_channels=7, kernel=5) as per problem statement.
  // The problem states %arg0 = conv1d_transpose.weight with shape [6x7x5]
  // So %arg0 shape is [in_channels=6, out_channels=7, kernel=5]

  // The input shape is [6,6,8] = [batch=6, in_channels=6, length=8]

  // For convolution in StableHLO:
