  // input: [b, i, d, h, w]
  // kernel: [i, o, kd, kh, kw] for normal conv, but for conv_transpose we swap input and output channels and use rhs_dilation
  // But stablehlo.convolution does not have a direct conv_transpose op.
  // ConvTranspose3d can be implemented as a convolution with lhs_dilation = stride and rhs_dilation = 1, swapping input/output channels in kernel.
  // So we do convolution with:
  // lhs = input %arg2: [6,3,16,7,7]
  // rhs = weight_transposed: [16,3,3,3,3] but we need kernel shape [o,i,kd,kh,kw] = [3,16,3,3,3] for conv
  // So we must transpose weight to [3,16,3,3,3] for conv, but we want conv_transpose, so we use lhs_dilation=stride=2, rhs_dilation=1, and swap input/output channels in kernel.

  // So we transpose weight to [16,3,3,3,3] (done above)
  // Use dimension_numbers = #conv<[b, i, d, h, w]x[o, i, kd, kh, kw]->[b, o, d, h, w]>
  // lhs_dilation = [2,2,2] (stride)
  // rhs_dilation = [1,1,1]
  // padding = [[1,1],[1,1],[1,1]]

  // Define dimension_numbers attribute
